    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.test\n\n### Description\n\nHi all,\n\nI recently starting mini.test, It has been a blast! I really enjoy the many conveniences provided. I was just getting started on hacking my own \"coverage\" script when it occurred to me that this might be something worth adding to the plugin. \n\nOne possible \"format\" this could be is a markdown-table with columns like \"test-name\", \"start_time\", \"test_args\", \"result\" where the rows are filled in from this particular run.\n\nSince I have some experience developing plugins I would volunteer to experiment with some sort of mvp. \nLet me know what you think, I am open to suggestions on what to include. \n",
