            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nSorry, what do you mean by \"coverage report\"? My first reaction is that it should describe which parts of the *source code* are covered by tests, which is the only meaning I have experience with. This functionality is *definitely* out of scope of 'mini.test' as it seems to be rather non-trivial to implement.\n\n> One possible \"format\" this could be is a markdown-table with columns like \"test-name\", \"start_time\", \"test_args\", \"result\" where the rows are filled in from this particular run.\n\nJudging by the column names it looks like you want a custom [reporter](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/dc1775613f672e6a804577945813353c5c4e6fe5/doc/mini-test.txt#L180-L181), which is already possible.",
